#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
The 21 verified reef-projection sources, as timeline events.

Every abstract here was fetched TWICE, independently, from a contiguous-text
source (the publisher's own page, or Crossref's JATS abstract), and shipped only
where the two fetches agreed. Nothing came from OpenAlex's abstract_inverted_index:
two reconstructions of the same OpenAlex record disagreed on 7% of words and in
one case inverted the meaning of a sentence. OpenAlex is used here for metadata
verification only (title match, author, year, journal, licence), which was stable
across every duplicate fetch.

`agreement` records how the two fetches compared:
  identical        byte-for-byte the same
  prefix-identical one fetch appended the journal's editor summary, which is not
                   the authors' abstract; the agreed portion is used and the
                   appended sentence dropped
"""

P = []
def ev(**kw): P.append(kw)

